levels had increased by 6.7 and 11.9 percent, respectively, in the paricalcitol group, as compared with 8.2 and 13.9 
percent, respectively, in the calcitriol group (P<0.001). The two-year survival rate among patients who switched from 
calcitriol to paricalcitol was 73 percent, as compared with 64 percent among those who switched from paricalcitol to 
calcitriol (P=0.04).   Conclusions Patients who receive paricalcitol while undergoing long-term hemodialysis appear to 
