  rats: (i) metastatic calcification of heart and aorta, and (ii) renal dysfunction with nephrocalcinosis, using the    
  same effective doses for hyperparathyroidism. OCT (1.25 and 6.25 μg/kg) or 1,25(OH)2D3 (0.125 and 0.625 μg/kg)        
  solutions were administered intravenously to subtotally nephrectomized (SNX) rats three times weekly for 2 weeks.     
