  patients undergoing haemodialysis for a follow-up of 61±23 months. The daily dose of alfacalcidol ranged from 0.25    
  to 1.5 μg, with a median of 0.5 μg. Results. The alfacalcidol users showed a lower risk of death from cardiovascular  
  disease than the non-users in a univariate Cox model [hazards ratio (HR) 0.287, 95% confidence interval (CI)          
  0.127–0.649, P=0.003], whereas the risk for death from non-cardiovascular disease was not different between the two   
  groups. Stepwise multivariate Cox analysis showed that cardiovascular mortality was significantly associated with     
  age, presence of diabetes mellitus and treatment with alfacalcidol (HR 0.377, 95% CI 0.246–0.578, P=0.022).           
  Conclusions. These results indicate that use of oral alfacalcidol was associated with reduced risk for                
