long-term dialysis. After adjustment for demographics; comorbidities; estimated kidney function; medications; and 
baseline levels of parathyroid hormone, calcium, and phosphorous, oral calcitriol use was associated with a 26% lower 
risk for death (95% confidence interval 5 to 42% lower; P = 0.016) and a 20% lower risk for death or dialysis (95% 
